The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue with one fix queued. Its own table says
otherwise, and the report bodies say more. Every report merged into #4471 belongs to exactly one
of the problems below. Each has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. The queued parser fix will not close the form-hint reports or the one-day moves.
Keep #4471 open until all three tickets are closed.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemSplit ticket={4471} {issues} />

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first.** Our tenants all write the day
first, so in the app, by email and through `booking-v2` forms, 7 April comes out as 4 July. This is
the fix already queued.

**`hint`: the `booking-v3` form tells people to type month first.** Its date field shows
`MM/DD/YYYY`, people follow it, and the form then reads their date day first. The parser
fix does not touch this: the hint or the form's reading has to change. Only form reports from
`booking-v3` tenants land here. Intake tags these by the reporter's browser, so its `hint` tag
and this group disagree; this group follows the tenant (`causes.ts`).

**`one-day-move`: the date moves by one day, not month for day.** "Invite says Tuesday 12 May.
Calendar says Monday 11 May." A client in Lisbon and one in Toronto got different days for one
meeting; an invite arrived before the booking was made. That is a time zone or midnight
conversion bug, not a parser one. The desk noted these reports (`desk-notes.json`) but
[CauseTable](/kb/incidents/4471) still counts them under `parser` by tenant, so they vanish
from view.

## What the desk table showed

For comparison, the table on the #4471 page, built from the same export:

